    "product_id": "d300519c-5084-484c-a93d-f7ae13f9c846",
    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 141142\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n442 AM PDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Breezy south-southwesterly wind gusts will continue through the \n  week with dry conditions and near-normal temperatures.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\n\nThe Desert Southwest will remain situated between an upper-level \ntrough across the Pacific Northwest and a ridge of high pressure \nacross the southern Plains. As a result, increased pressure \ngradients aloft will return gusty south-southwest winds to the \nregion each day through at least midweek. Expect gust speeds \ngenerally between 25 and 35 mph, though can't rule out 40 mph\nspeeds in isolated instances and/or in the higher terrain. \nOtherwise, expect mostly dry conditions and temperatures near-\nnormal. Near-normal for this time of year for desert valleys is \nin the upper-90s to lower-100s. Mid-to-late week, confidence \ndecreases. Ensemble means show a closed area of low pressure \npushing into the southwestern Great Basin Wednesday and Thursday, \nthen eventually meandering across the southern Great Basin heading\ninto the weekend. The associated upper-level jet overhead should \nprovide ample instability to our western zones. When combined with\nPWATs between 0.75 and 1.00 inches, portions of northwestern \nArizona could see a return of scattered showers and thunderstorms.\nWill continue to monitor as we get closer.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Gusty\nsouth-southwesterly winds will dominate for a majority of the \nforecast period, with gusts to 20-25KT expected through sunset \nthis evening. Thereafter, sustained speeds will remain around 10KT\nthrough Tuesday morning, when winds are expected to back to the \nsouth. VFR conditions prevail, with temperatures briefly reaching \na high of 100 degrees around 23Z-00Z.\n\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCalifornia...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Winds across much of\nthe region will become elevated and gusty out of the south-\nsouthwest by mid- to late morning, with gusts to 20-25KT common \nthrough this evening before gradually diminishing. Exceptions \ninclude the western Mojave Desert/KDAG, where west-northwesterly \nwinds are not expected to shift to the southwest until early \nevening, with gusts continuing through much of the night, as well \nas the northern Owens Valley/KBIH, where winds generally follow \ntypical daily patterns with speeds around 10KT or less. VFR \nconditions will prevail, with isolated thunderstorms expected over\nportions of northwestern Arizona this afternoon that are unlikely\nto cause any impacts at area terminals.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Soulat \nAVIATION...Phillipson\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
